{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Your father's brother's wife.</b> She is reckoned as your aunt. And behold, [consider] Hanamel my uncle [Jeremiah 32:7]. Now what will those who rely on the commandment upon the Torah alone do, for Scripture did not forbid a wife of a maternal uncle, nor a father's mother, nor a mother's mother? Therefore we need the received tradition. It is possible that he did not mention a wife of a maternal uncle because we learn it from a wife of a paternal uncle, and he mentioned her in the section of Kedoshim. Also, those [women] mentioned [in the tradition] whom Scripture did not mention — the matter concerns that which exists [in practice]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Jeremiah 32:8 (הנה חנמאל דודי) to show that a paternal uncle's wife is called an aunt; the verse reference is implicit. The phrase 'הסומכים במצות על התורה לבדה' refers to Karaites who rely on Scripture alone without rabbinic tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:42.977110725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}